This folder contains artifacts derived from three lineprinter documents, and the
distributed game contains one derived from the fourth:

The file >user_dir_dir>MED>Kaiser>Lippard>exp_dir>explore.basic.1,
   printed by Lippard.Scouting.a on 06/27/80 2047.7 mst Fri, 36 pages,
   2,135 lines. Kaiser.MED was Wendell Garrett "Garry" Kaiser
   (b. August 2, 1945, Kansas City, MO, d. August 26, 2021, Phoenix,
   AZ), who worked for Honeywell Marketing and Education and was a
   close family friend; he was probably providing me with disk space
   since our "quota" was limited. "shelf506 DVCP" was a shelf in
   Honeywell's Deer Valley Computer Park at 23rd Ave. and Peoria;
   printouts would be made at the Camelback Road Facility (I-17 and
   Camelback) where the Multics System M was located and delivered to
   other Honeywell locations via its internal mail. This is Multics
   Basic version 5.3 of the game.

The file
   >user_dir_dir>MED>Kaiser>Lippard>explore_dir>explore.data.explore,
   printed by Lippard.Multics.a on 07/14/80 0207.8 mst Mon, 12 pages,
   667 lines. This was a listing of the game database version 6.0, an
   aspirational new version for which the program was never completed.

The file >udd>sct>sed>explore.play, printed by Lippard.Scouting.a on
   10/18/82 0155.7 mst Mon, 14 pages, 646 lines (and sent to "Shelf
   700" at DVCP). "sed" was Steve Ditton, sct was a short name for
   Scouting, the Multics System M project ID of the
   Honeywell-sponsored Explorers Post 414. This was a play-through of
   game version 4.3. This transcript contains some abbreviations and
   modifications from the original.

The winners.data distributed on this site was also an artifact from
   lineprinter output, the file
   >user_dir_dir>MED>Kaiser>Lippard>explore_dir>temp>winners.data,
   printed by Lippard.Scouting.a on 11/03/80 0127.4 mst Mon, 1 page,
   17 lines (and sent to "Sta W DVCP" unlike the other listings.

Everything else in the repo was reconstructed from these artifacts, memory, and
inference from these artifacts.